// §249 — INDONESIAN. Keyed by the English source (normalized innerHTML for rich
// blocks, text for plate labels); see src/explain-i18n.js for why.
//
// Vocabulary is the SAME register tier one's chrome uses (src/i18n.js):
// mesin jam, eskapemen jangkar Swiss, roda eskapemen, jangkar, balans, pegas
// rambut, pegas utama, tabung pegas, fusee, rantai, pinion, mahkota, roda
// kolom, governor. One movement cannot have two names for a part.
//
// Standard spelling (EYD): plain ASCII letters, no diacritics, so the pages
// need no line-height rule — Vietnamese's vertical question is answered by
// the character inventory. Indonesian attaches -nya and the di-/me-/-kan
// affixes with no space, so the hidden .gloss-variants rows list those forms.
//
// NUMBERS AND <code> ARE NOT TRANSLATED — they are the source constants this
// page exists to quote. Emphasis the English carries as CAPITALS rides the
// wording, never an added tag. "dimodelkan" vs "disimulasikan" tracks the
// repo's modelled/simulated distinction exactly; HONESTY.id gates it, and the
// bare noun «model» is deliberately not the honesty word.
